From: LineageOS Linux HDMI contributors
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] glamor: prefer render node for DRI3 clients

Backport the current upstream Xorg behavior to 21.1.24. DRI3 clients should
receive the unprivileged render node when one exists; opening the primary node
instead requires legacy DRM authentication and fails when Xorg itself holds a
lease fd rather than the DRM master.

diff --git a/glamor/glamor_egl.c b/glamor/glamor_egl.c
index 525b1f4c7..b5f8501ef 100644
--- a/glamor/glamor_egl.c
+++ b/glamor/glamor_egl.c
@@ -926,4 +926,6 @@ glamor_egl_screen_init(ScreenPtr screen, struct glamor_context *glamor_ctx)
          */
-        glamor_egl->device_path = drmGetDeviceNameFromFd2(glamor_egl->fd);
-
+        glamor_egl->device_path = drmGetRenderDeviceNameFromFd(glamor_egl->fd);
+        if (!glamor_egl->device_path)
+            glamor_egl->device_path = drmGetDeviceNameFromFd2(glamor_egl->fd);
+
         if (!dri3_screen_init(screen, &glamor_dri3_info)) {
